cp-graphql-basic-001.example:
```graphql
# A query asks for exactly the fields it needs:
query GetProduct($id: ID!) {
  getProduct(id: $id) {
    id
    name
    price
  }
}

# The response mirrors the query's shape:
# { "data": { "getProduct": { "id": "cel-1", "name": "iPhone 12", "price": 1500000 } } }
```

cp-graphql-basic-003.example:
```graphql
# schema.graphql — the contract
type Query {
  getProduct(id: ID!): Product
}

# A query against it
query {
  getProduct(id: "cel-apple-iphone-12-128gb") { id name price }
}

# The resolver (APPSYNC_JS) decides how to fetch it:
#   request()  -> DynamoDB GetItem on the id
#   response() -> map the item to the Product fields
```

